# EMIR margin eligibility — intensional rules (Datalog Horn clauses in N3).
# TC-MEGA-FIBO-01 lane L38. STRATIFICATION LAYER 2.
#
# Bounded stratification (closed-world completeness, binding addendum item 1):
#   Layer 0  extensional scenario facts (twins/, scenario data): all reg:
#            ground atoms. Negation is NEVER taken over layer 0-incomplete
#            predicates; reg: predicates here are read under the closed-world
#            assumption of the layer-0 fact base being saturated and finite.
#   Layer 1  rules/saccr_netting_set_rules.n3: positive Horn clauses only;
#            saturates to its least Herbrand model (finite: range-restricted
#            heads over finite layer-0 facts).
#   Layer 2  THIS FILE. Negation-as-failure appears ONLY via log:notIncludes
#            over formulas whose predicates are fully computed by layer 1
#            (reg:SACCRRecognizedNettingSet, reg:nettingSetMember,
#            reg:coNettedWith) or ground layer-0 atoms.
#            There is no negation over any layer-2 head predicate, so the
#            stratification is acyclic and evaluation is a single ordered
#            fixpoint pass per layer: terminates by construction.
#
# Comparison atoms use the sql-rdf Rec section 4 operator tokens (= != < <=
# > >=) carried as ngn:comparison over xsd:decimal literals, matching the
# operator enum in src/sql_ast.rs Operator::from_token.
#
# NAMESPACE + OPERATOR RECONCILIATION (WO-13 decisions):
#   reg:  first-class scenario-local namespace of this self-contained
#         mega ontology; not mapped onto or renamed under repo-canonical
#         surfaces. Declared above and in every generated shapes/ header.
#   log: / math: are the standard CWM/swap vocabularies (external, stable
#         IRIs), used as the N3 spelling of this scenario's rule layer.
#   Canonical operator form: the section-4 token `<` / the sql:LessThan
#         axiom IRI. math:lessThan below is the N3 spelling of exactly that
#         operator (swap/math#lessThan over xsd:decimal <=> `<` token); pick
#         the token form in any future compiler admission lane. No rename of
#         math:lessThan in N3 -- the correspondence is documented, not
#         silently rewritten.

@prefix reg: <http://graphlaw.org/ns/mega/fibo/reg#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2.1  EMIR-eligible: a recognized netting set whose jurisdiction is
#       an EMIR scope and whose members are all CCP clearing members.
{ ?ns a reg:SACCRRecognizedNettingSet ;
      reg:nettingSetJurisdiction ?j .
  ?h reg:ccpMemberOf ?ccp .
  ?ns reg:nettingSetMember ?h .
  ?scenario log:notIncludes { ?ns reg:emirExclusionFlag ?x . } . }
=> { ?ns a reg:EMIREligibleNettingSet . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2.2  Margin obligation arises when posted variation margin is below
#       the agreement threshold (numeric comparison, >= semantics).
{ ?ma a reg:MarginAgreement ;
      reg:marginThreshold ?thr ;
      reg:variationMargin ?vm .
  ?vm math:lessThan ?thr . }
=> { ?ma a reg:MarginCallObligation . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2.3  Eligibility exclusion: a holder outside all recognized netting
#       sets is NOT margin-eligible under EMIR (negation on the
#       completed layer-1 predicate reg:nettingSetMember).
{ ?h a reg:LEIHolder ;
     reg:isDaEligible true .
  ?scenario log:notIncludes { ?ns reg:nettingSetMember ?h . } . }
=> { ?h reg:emirMarginIneligible ?h . } .

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2.4  Threshold breach isJurisdiction-specific: a margin agreement
#       breaches when its threshold exceeds the jurisdiction cap and
#       it carries no cap waiver.
{ ?ma a reg:MarginAgreement ;
      reg:marginThreshold ?thr ;
      reg:party ?h .
  ?h reg:jurisdiction ?j .
  ?cap reg:capFor ?j ;
       reg:capAmount ?c .
  ?c math:lessThan ?thr .
  ?scenario log:notIncludes { ?ma reg:capWaiver true . } . }
=> { ?ma a reg:ThresholdBreach . } .
